\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces (a) Freezing-point error on single solutes not used in the fit (log scale). The blue band marks molecules where the constant transfers and the red band where it fails. (b) Error on the water--glycerol--NaCl liquidus \cite  {shepard}. All three models predict from single-solute data. (c) Post hoc constant each molecule would need on its own (fits $\le 20$\,wt\%). Open symbols mark depressions below 3\,K, where the constant is weakly determined. The dashed line is the glycerol constant used in the blind tests.}}{4}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:results}{{3}{4}{(a) Freezing-point error on single solutes not used in the fit (log scale). The blue band marks molecules where the constant transfers and the red band where it fails. (b) Error on the water--glycerol--NaCl liquidus \cite {shepard}. All three models predict from single-solute data. (c) Post hoc constant each molecule would need on its own (fits $\le 20$\,wt\%). Open symbols mark depressions below 3\,K, where the constant is weakly determined. The dashed line is the glycerol constant used in the blind tests}{figure.caption.4}{}}
